    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** Iteration granularity. One mega-prompt produces a page-sized surprise; three small prompts produce three small, judgeable changes. The AI on this level is configured to make only one change per request, so students feel the rhythm: ask, look, decide, repeat.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What were your three steps? Why that order?\"\r\n- \"Did any change surprise you? Was it easier to catch because it was small?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may bundle several changes into one prompt - the AI will do only one; use it as the teachable moment\r\n- Students may not look at the preview between steps - ask them what change #2 actually did before they send #3\r\n",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
  },
